      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Choosing between an SGLT2 inhibitor and a GLP-1 receptor agonist as a first-line or early treatment for type 2 diabetes depends heavily on individual health risks, organ protection needs, and treatment goals . While metformin has historically been the traditional first-line choice, major diabetes guidelines (such as the ADA and EASD) now recommend tailoring first-line or early therapy based on specific cardiorenal profiles and patient characteristics.",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "depends heavily on individual health risks, organ protection needs, and treatment goals"
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          0,
          1,
          2
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Core Comparison"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "SGLT2 Inhibitors (e.g., empagliflozin, dapagliflozin)",
            "list": [
              {
                "snippet": "Form: Mostly oral tablets."
              },
              {
                "snippet": "Key Strengths: Superior for heart failure (reducing hospitalizations and mortality) and chronic kidney disease (slowing hard renal decline)."
              },
              {
                "snippet": "Blood Sugar & Weight: Effective HbA1c reduction (~0.7%\u20131.0%) and moderate weight loss."
              },
              {
                "snippet": "Main Side Effects: Genitourinary infections (yeast/UTIs), volume depletion, risk of diabetic ketoacidosis (DKA).",
                "reference_indexes": [
                  1,
                  3,
                  5,
                  6,
                  7,
                  8
                ]
              }
            ],
            "reference_indexes": [
              1,
              3,
              5,
              6,
              7,
              8
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "GLP-1 Receptor Agonists (e.g., semaglutide, dulaglutide)",
            "list": [
              {
                "snippet": "Form: Mostly subcutaneous injections (though oral semaglutide is available)."
              },
              {
                "snippet": "Key Strengths: Superior for weight loss and lowering major adverse cardiovascular events (ASCVD, stroke prevention)."
              },
              {
                "snippet": "Blood Sugar & Weight: More potent HbA1c and substantial weight-loss reductions."
              },
              {
                "snippet": "Main Side Effects: Gastrointestinal issues (nausea, vomiting, diarrhea), potential thyroid C-cell tumor warnings (in animal studies).",
                "reference_indexes": [
                  1,
                  3,
                  4,
                  5,
                  6,
                  9
                ]
              }
            ],
            "reference_indexes": [
              1,
              3,
              4,
              5,
              6,
              9
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "When to Choose Which"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Choose an SGLT2 Inhibitor first if: You have or are at high risk for heart failure (especially with reduced ejection fraction) or chronic kidney disease .",
            "reference_indexes": [
              1,
              10
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Choose a GLP-1 Receptor Agonist first if: Your primary goals are significant weight loss or protection against atherosclerotic cardiovascular disease / stroke .",
            "reference_indexes": [
              1,
              9
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Combination Therapy: In many high-risk patients, clinicians may prescribe both classes together because their mechanisms are complementary (addressing glucose, weight, heart, and kidneys via different pathways).",
            "reference_indexes": [
              1,
              11
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Could you share what specific health conditions (like heart disease, kidney issues, or weight goals) or current medications you are managing so I can provide more relevant details?"
      }
    ],
